# Wrela Rust conventions

Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`docs/design/locked-decisions.md`](../../docs/design/locked-decisions.md) first.

## Phase boundaries

- Compiler phases return data (`Diagnostic`, `LexedFile`, `DiscoverResult`, etc.).
- Only `command.rs` writes to stdout/stderr or chooses process exit codes.
- Do not add `println!` / `eprintln!` in `src/` outside `command.rs`.

## Data and immutability

- Phase outputs are owned structs; later phases read them, they do not mutate in place.
- Prefer explicit inputs over global state.

## Spans and source

- `Span` uses `u32` byte offsets into `SourceFile` text.
- Spans must start and end on UTF-8 character boundaries (`is_char_boundary`).
- Tokens and trivia store `Span` only — no copied lexeme text in token structs.

## Diagnostics

- Use `Diagnostic::error(span, message)` for recoverable issues; continue when the plan says to.
- Use unspanned diagnostics when no valid `FileId` exists (e.g. root load failure).
- Merge order must stay deterministic when combining phase diagnostics.

## Dependencies and safety

- Do not add `[dependencies]` without a new ADR in `docs/design/`.
- No `unsafe`, `todo!()`, or `unimplemented!()` in production `src/`.

## Testing

- Unit tests: colocated in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in the same file.
- Integration tests: `tests/*.rs` using the public crate API only (`use wrela::...`).
- Fixtures live under `fixtures/`; prefer real `.wrela` files over inline strings for integration coverage.

## Quality gate

There is no CI. Run `./scripts/quality-gate.sh` before claiming work complete.

## Plan work

- Implement plans on a **feature branch** in the main repo (`git checkout -b feat/<name>` from `main`). Do not use a worktree by default.
- Subagents must not run `cargo` or `./scripts/quality-gate.sh`; the orchestrator verifies sequentially (see `.cursor/rules/plan-orchestration.mdc`).
- Complete Phase A before handoff; fix **every** Phase A and user-feedback item (all severities) unless explicitly disagreed and documented; merge after feedback is fully resolved (see multi-model review skill).
